Among the three alternatives, `0result.sql` is the safest and therefore the correct choice.

• It uses `COUNT(DISTINCT dm.movie_id)` so the movie count cannot be inflated by accidental duplicate joins (e.g. if the ratings table ever contained multiple rows per movie).  
• It keeps every movie in the calculation instead of discarding titles that simply lack a rating or duration (unlike `2result.sql`, which would under‑count).  
• It is syntactically simpler than `1result.sql` (no verbose quoting) while still returning the same, accurate result set.

```plaintext
0result.sql
```